  "translation": "Good morning, Mrs. Georgescu. I see you came with your daughter. Good morning, Doctor. Yes, Ana brought me, because I don't remember everything I need. Good morning. Mom lost her diabetes tablets again last week and her blood sugar was high. How high? In the morning two hundred ten, last night one hundred eighty. I measured it with her device. Mrs. Georgescu, what tablets are you taking now? Metformin, I think one thousand, in the morning and evening. But sometimes I forget the evening one. And how is the left foot? Last time you had a small wound on the heel. It still hurts and turns red in the evening. Let me check. The wound hasn't closed and the skin around it is red. You need to see a surgeon. Where do we go? I will refer you to surgery, to the outpatient clinic of the county hospital. Try to get an appointment during the next week. I will take care of the appointment, I'll call you tomorrow morning. Very well. Until then, daily dressing with physiological serum and betadine. The community assistant can come to your home to show you how to do it. It would be very helpful, I work until five. I will inform the community assistant, Mrs. Ioana, to visit you on Monday afternoon. And with the tablets, what do I do, because I keep forgetting them? I recommend a box of pills for each day of the week. Ana, please prepare it for her on Sunday evening for the whole week. Sure, I will buy it from the pharmacy today. I also want a glycosylated hemoglobin and a urine test. You do them at the lab until Friday. We will do them on Thursday, because I have free time. Come back on November 20th at eleven o'clock with the results and with the medical letter from the surgeon. November 20th, at eleven. Ana, please write it down, please. I noted. Thank you very much, Doctor. You're welcome. If fever appears or the foot swells, come immediately."
